---
import ClosingCTA from "../../components/ClosingCTA.astro";
import CoreDiagram from "../../components/CoreDiagram.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import { site } from "../../data/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
	description="Learn about SolidCore, the Rust port of NVIDIA’s SMLib geometry library. Browse port progress, test results, and development status."
	title="SolidCore · A geometry kernel written in Rust"
>
	<section class="page-intro container intro-grid">
		<div>
			<p class="eyebrow">SOLIDCORE / GEOMETRY KERNEL</p>
			<h1>A geometry kernel<br>written in Rust.</h1>
			<p class="lead">
				SolidCore is a Rust port of SMLib, an open-source C++ geometry library
				released by NVIDIA. It is being developed for use in SolidCraft.
			</p>
			<div class="actions">
				<a class="button primary" href="/solidcore/progress/">
					View port progress<Icon size={18} />
				</a>
				<a class="text-link" href={site.kernel}>
					View the source<Icon name="external" size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
		<CoreDiagram />
	</section>
	<section class="section section-alt">
		<div class="container story-grid">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">BOUNDARY REPRESENTATION (B-REP)</p>
				<h2>How SolidCore<br>represents a solid.</h2>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<p>
					A boundary representation describes a solid through its shells, faces,
					loops, edges, and vertices. Geometry defines their shapes; topology
					defines how they connect.
				</p>
				<p>
					The editor converts this geometry into a mesh of triangles for
					display. The mesh is the on-screen representation; the B-rep stores
					the underlying geometry and connections.
				</p>
				<p>
					SolidCore’s scope covers the geometry and operation layers: NURBS
					math, curves, surfaces, topology, intersections, and the foundations
					for modeling operations.
				</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="section">
		<div class="container story-grid">
			<div>
				<p class="eyebrow">DEVELOPMENT STATUS</p>
				<h2>Still in development.</h2>
				<p class="lead">
					SolidCore’s components are being ported and tested against the
					original C++ code. Complete modeling operations and integration into
					the editor are still in development.
				</p>
			</div>
			<div class="prose">
				<h3>What works so far?</h3>
				<p>
					The reviewed source includes math, NURBS, and curve components, with
					surfaces and topology under way. Complete operations such as creating
					primitives, booleans, and fillets are not ready yet.
				</p>
				<p>SolidCraft v0.12.0 uses Truck at its geometry-kernel boundary.</p>
				<a
					class="text-link"
					href={`${site.kernel}/blob/16c5ad9cec67741ab00a41b75b18dfa7985e70ef/README.md`}
				>
					Read the source status<Icon name="external" size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="section core-section">
		<div class="container">
			<div class="section-heading">
				<div>
					<p class="eyebrow">PORT STATUS AND TEST RESULTS</p>
					<h2>Browse the port<br>and its test results.</h2>
				</div>
				<a class="text-link" href="/solidcore/progress/">
					View progress dashboard<Icon size={18} />
				</a>
			</div>
			<div class="process">
				<div>
					<span class="mono">01 / UNITS</span>
					<h3>Unit status.</h3>
					<p>
						See which units are verified, partially ported, claimed, blocked, or
						unstarted.
					</p>
					<a
						class="text-link"
						href="/solidcore/progress/units/"
						style="margin-top:16px"
					>
						Browse units →
					</a>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span class="mono">02 / COMPARISON</span>
					<h3>Rust vs. C++ tests.</h3>
					<p>Compare results from the Rust port and original C++ code.</p>
					<a
						class="text-link"
						href="/solidcore/progress/"
						style="margin-top:16px"
					>
						Read the overview →
					</a>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span class="mono">03 / UPSTREAM</span>
					<h3>Upstream bugs.</h3>
					<p>Read bugs found in the original C++ code during porting.</p>
					<a
						class="text-link"
						href="/solidcore/progress/issues/"
						style="margin-top:16px"
					>
						Browse upstream issues →
					</a>
				</div>
				<div>
					<span class="mono">04 / INTERSECTIONS</span>
					<h3>Intersection tests.</h3>
					<p>
						See how Rust and C++ handle the surface-intersection test cases.
					</p>
					<a
						class="text-link"
						href="/solidcore/progress/ssi/"
						style="margin-top:16px"
					>
						View intersection tests →
					</a>
				</div>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
	<section class="container" style="padding-block:48px">
		<div class="notice">
			<strong>License & attribution.</strong>
			<br>
			SolidCore is licensed under Apache-2.0 and includes notices for the
			original SMLib code. It is an independent project, not affiliated with or
			endorsed by NVIDIA.{" "}<a href="/licenses/#solidcore">
				Read the attribution.
			</a>
		</div>
	</section>
	<ClosingCTA />
</BaseLayout>
